<OlspLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://olsp.profitandprivilege.com/blog/affiliate-marketing-vs-mlm/" tocLinks={tocLinks}>
<section id="difference"><h1>Affiliate Marketing vs MLM: The Questions That Matter</h1><p>Affiliate marketing and multi-level marketing can overlap in how products are promoted, but the structure and obligations vary by program. The name alone does not tell you whether an offer is a good fit.</p><p>Compare the product, customer demand, compensation rules, required purchases, and how much of the expected income depends on recruiting others.</p></section>
<GoldMasterQuote />
<section id="questions"><h2>Questions worth answering before joining</h2><ul><li>What does a customer receive for the initial payment?</li><li>Can a participant earn from genuine customer sales without recruiting?</li><li>Are recurring costs and cancellation terms easy to find?</li><li>What training and support are included?</li><li>Are income claims documented and realistic?</li></ul><p>A transparent answer is more valuable than a persuasive label. Keep your notes and make the decision only after you understand the complete path.</p></section>
<section id="olsp"><h2>Review the OLSP structure directly</h2><p>For the official explanation of OLSP training and the available next steps, review the <a href="/olsp-livebinar/?utm_source=article&utm_medium=content&utm_campaign=affiliate_vs_mlm">Live Webinar</a> after completing your own checklist.</p></section>
</OlspLayout>
